'''Sir Metal Seal''' (メタルゴマさま, ''Metaru Goma-sama'', '''Sir Metal Goma''') is a [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of [[Sir Seal]] that appears in [[Legend Stages]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Sir Metal Seal
|image = E 059.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[Dead Falls|Sub-chapter 18 - Dead Falls]]
|money drop = 1,155¢ - 4,562¢
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Floating Bus Stop|Sub-chapter 19 - Floating Bus Stop]]
}}

==Enemy==
Sir Metal Seal has medium movement speed, a faster attack rate than [[Sir Seal]], higher attack power and very high health for a Metal enemy (2.75 times that of [[Super Metal Hippoe]]). Like all Metal enemies, Sir Metal Seal only takes one damage from all attacks except for [[Critical Hit]]s, making him incredibly tanky and difficult to neutralize.

==Strategy==
Sir Metal Seal's high health can often allow him to take a beating and push easily. [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]] works great in earlier encounters because he has decent range and can easily be stacked, but tougher Sir Metal Seals will require more advanced units such as [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]], [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]], [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]] and [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Ballet Cat]] to take down.

As Sir Metal Seal has immense stats for a Metal enemy, crowd-controllers such as [[Clockwork Cat (Rare Cat)|Puppetmaster Cat]], [[Drumcorps Cat (Rare Cat)|Banner Cat]] and [[Hoop Cat (Rare Cat)|Showoff Cat]] are highly recommended to help keep Sir Metal Seal from advancing forward, thus buying more time and opportunities for your Critical Hitters to attack. Later in the game, you can also use specialist meatshields like [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] or [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern Cat]] to ensure he doesn't immediately destroy your [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal units]].

Nearly any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] or [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]] with Critical Hits or anti-Metal abilities is effective against Sir Metal Seal. [[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Tesalan Pasalan]] is of particular note because his Critical Hit can OHKO Sir Metal Seal, though his Critical chance of 10% (20% in [[True Form]], 30% with maxed [[Talents]]) is too low for him to be relied upon as your only Critter in most scenarios.

While [[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Paladin Cat]] is already good against Sir Metal Seal in his own right, his level 1 Attack Buff Talent gives a level 50 Paladin Cat just enough damage to knockback a 300% Sir Metal Seal with one Crit. Unlock this Talent if you often struggle with Sir Metal Seal in late-game stages, but do not invest more than 1 level into it.

